{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"code":["let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self, CheckedOut.self])","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write-through."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, with one ","type":"text"},{"code":"write()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"power loss too (","type":"text"},{"code":"fsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the app moves to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"background or terminates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What is kept.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Only events of the types in "},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which conform to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other, are never written, and produce no drop report, but are lost if the app ends first."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record’s context is not kept: a recovered record is in the top-level "},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as its span ended with the earlier run."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deleting."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. There is no compaction: a segment kept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for one undelivered record keeps its delivered ones too."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bound."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The log never holds more than ","type":"text"},{"code":"byteBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered yields a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","isActive":true},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"text":". A record too large for an empty log","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is kept in memory only.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Recovery.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comes back with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRedelivered"},{"text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Newer versions.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store share its log."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"title":"SegmentStore","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SegmentStore.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L47"},"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\